# Logging & Exception Standards

## Java Service Standards
- **Logger Initialization:**
  ```java
  private static final CampXLogger logger = CampXLoggerFactory.getLogger(MyService.class);
  ```
- **Flow Tracking & Tracing:**
  ```java
  FlowTracker tracker = logger.flow("OPERATION_NAME", correlationId);
  try { ... } finally { tracker.close(); }
  ```
- **RFC 7807 Problem Details:** Throw domain exceptions with HTTP status and machine code:
  ```java
  throw new LifecycleException(422, "REMARKS_TOO_SHORT", "Remarks must contain at least 5 characters");
  ```
- **No Swallowed Exceptions or Console Output:**
  - Never use `System.out.println` or bare `e.printStackTrace()` in production code.
  - Never catch `Exception` and silently swallow without logging or rethrowing.

## Next.js Frontend Standards
- **BFF Error Propagation:** Return RFC 7807 JSON with status from upstream gateway:
  ```ts
  const res = await fetch(`${GATEWAY_URL}/api/v1/...`, { ... });
  const text = await res.text();
  return new NextResponse(text, { status: res.status, headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  ```
- **Client Parsing:** Parse problem details using standard helper:
  ```ts
  function parseProblemDetails(text: string) {
    try {
      const p = JSON.parse(text);
      return p.detail || p.title || p.message || text;
    } catch { return text; }
  }
  ```
